All the punches he's taking, yes.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:16:01.760
Yeah, so that's the Ring King minigame, and that's mostly the game in a nutshell, too, is, like, you know, if you weren't blowing on the cartridge to get it to work, you were probably blowing your character to get him back in the ring for the next round.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:11.700
I don't really have too much more to say about this game because I wasn't, like, I don't know, I wasn't a huge fan of how the actual boxing mechanic works.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.920
This game, presentation-wise, is great.

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.340
Graphics for an early NES game, pretty cool, too.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:18.900
I like the pseudo-3D thing.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.660
It just doesn't have enough, it's not exciting enough.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.900
The punches lack weight.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:35.020
I mean, I know that it's hard for a game to have weight at this stage, but there have been a lot of games that we've played on the NES so far that feel a lot more tactile than this.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:38.140
And I have no idea how you do the special moves.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:40.460
The special moves are pretty cool to pull off, like, when you...

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:41.920
I think it's a distance thing, actually.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:48.440
Is it? So I think it's actually the distance you have from the opponent, it's just hitting the normal attack button.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:55.260
And to be honest, even if you can't perform them in the game, if you do see them in, like, a video, they are pretty cool, the special attacks.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:17:05.020
So I think, like, that, again, like, just another cool presentation thing that just gets blurred somewhere in the actual gameplay because it's harder to achieve than it should be.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:06.880
Or, you know what it reminds me of?

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:16.040
In tag team wrestling, when you have to, like, when you grapple someone and then select through a menu very quickly what grapple move you're going to use to them.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.260
You know, like, it's like, no, that's just not the way to, like, make it a directional thing.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.160
Make it a, you know, make it a combo of buttons.

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:28.540
Exactly. You know, don't make it, oh, if you're at this distance, like, fill up a meter for the special move.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.980
These things have all been thought out way ahead of this.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:35.700
So I think we're going to finalize these thoughts in the Essential Games list.

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:40.220
Okay, Essential Games list time.

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:45.260
And, Sean, I feel like you were heading in one direction when you were going on your rant right before this.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.140
So why don't you just finish that rant up?

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:51.040
Yeah, this game isn't good.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:54.080
There are some cool things that you can do.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:18:01.400
It's sort of like a metagame where it's, you can keep records and you sort of have some attachments to your character.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:06.200
You're not just boxing with random guys, but the boxing itself is very lackluster.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.180
So it is a pass.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:13.400
This game is different enough from Mike Tyson's Punch-Out!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:17.800
That, you know, it didn't, like, it wasn't copying that at all.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.920
It was actually trying a different approach at doing boxing on the NES.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:26.300
But, in my opinion, especially because Mike Tyson's Punch-Out!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:27.600
is coming out before the end of 87,

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:33.340
this is a complete pass because it's going to be obsolete even sooner than, like, we could say,

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.380
oh yeah, Fight Night, definitely play that instead.

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:37.460
Because we're always looking at the modern approach.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.980
But even if you look back then, this game should have been, like, a,

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.260
especially knowing it came out in 85 for the arcade,

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:46.580
this should have been one of Data East's first game to the NES.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:53.660
That's kind of like an early 86 or, you know, early 87 even, because now we're in September.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:58.940
It's like, for this game to come out now, I just don't think it, I think it missed its opportunity.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:02.540
It was probably better left at the arcade back in 1985.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:08.360
But I could see the appeal for the, you know, for the North American audience who was big on boxing at the time.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:12.020
So I'm sure this thing sold okay by all metrics.

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:16.600
But it's overall just not a game I'm going to boot up again.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.560
And it's not a game I would recommend to anybody.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.600
So, not essential.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:24.000
Yeah. I'm sort of sorry that it was this quick.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.640
This game doesn't have too much to it.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:33.080
Yeah, and I think even, and what's funny is, is, like, we've talked a lot about what makes this game good.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:35.500
Like, we didn't give it too much criticism while we were talking about it.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:38.840
So I think that's pretty much everything that you could say about this game.

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:46.300
You know? We talked about the RPG mechanics and stuff like that, but, like, you know, of moving your speed and stamina and punch.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.320
But as we also explained, there's just not really a lot to that.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:58.540
Like, sure, you can work on those stats and they move up, but, you know, I would argue that the progression system in Rygar was a lot cooler and more progressive.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:19:59.740
Yes, it was.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:03.320
Okay. So that's this episode of Nostalgia.

